analysis.fix_plan:
1) Retrieve the workflow definition JSON.
2) Locate actions["Condition"].inputs.expression (the Condition/If expression). It currently contains an endsWith(<leftArg>, <suffix>) call where <leftArg> can be null.
3) Update the expression to guard against null by coercing or defaulting the left operand to an empty string and optionally ensuring it’s not empty before evaluating. For example, replace:
   @endsWith(<leftArg>, '<suffix>')
   with:
   @and(not(empty(<leftArg>)), endsWith(string(coalesce(<leftArg>, '')), '<suffix>'))
   Example when checking a file name from the trigger body:
   @and(not(empty(triggerBody()?['fileName'])), endsWith(string(coalesce(triggerBody()?['fileName'], '')), '.csv'))
4) Save the updated definition and redeploy the Logic App.
5) Re-run a failed instance or a test run to verify the Condition no longer errors when the property is missing/null.
6) (Optional hardening) If case-insensitive suffix checks are desired, wrap the left operand with toLower():
   @and(not(empty(<leftArg>)), endsWith(toLower(string(coalesce(<leftArg>, ''))), toLower('<suffix>')))
